    "breadcrumb": "Dukungan Swing Catalyst \u003e Perangkat Keras",
    "content": "Cara menggunakan Foresight GC2 \u0026 HMT Launch Monitor dengan Swing Catalyst Pengenalan Artikel dukungan ini menjelaskan cara menggunakan Foresight GC2 dengan Swing Catalyst.\nCatatan: Jika Anda ingin menggunakan FSX bersama GC2, data HMT tidak disediakan dan Anda perlu memulai FSX terlebih dahulu lalu memulai Swing Catalyst, dan pilih FSX Sim dalam Pengaturan Swing Catalyst.\nWarning Mulai dari versi 10.1.1 dari Swing Catalyst, integrasi GC2 akan dinonaktifkan secara default untuk mencegah masalah dengan FSX 2020 menutup saat menjalankan Swing Catalyst.\nJika Anda memiliki GC2 dan ingin terus menggunakannya dengan Swing Catalyst, integrasi harus diaktifkan dari file pengaturan (lihat bagian pemecahan masalah di bawah).\nPersyaratan Komputer dengan port USB gratis atau WiFi (terpisah dari koneksi internet).\nLisensi dengan dukungan untuk kamera streaming langsung, kamera web, atau kamera kecepatan tinggi.\nSwing Catalyst 4.0 atau lebih baru\nImportant: Computer Recommendations.\nSwing Catalyst integrates both with the GC2 and the add-on unit, HMT.\nTo use the GC2 alongside the Foresight Simulator software (FR-1, FSX, FSX 2020 etc), Foresight Simulator must be selected in Swing Catalyst’s launch monitor settings.\nNote: If you are unfamiliar with Swing Catalyst’s launch monitor settings and how to use a launch monitor as a capture trigger please see our support article before continuing.\nDirect Connection (no FSX integration): This connection method connects to the unit directly without the need to run FSX side by side. If you have a HMT unit, Swing Catalyst will pick up club data as well.\nConfiguration Steps GC2 Support page (drivers, firmware and user manuals)\nFollow the Foresight GC2 installation guide (see link above), and install the GC2 USB Drivers. Make sure you select the correct version depending on your Windows version.\nEnsure the GC2 is using the latest firmware version\nWith the GC2 off, connect the GC2 to your computer with the USB cable, then turn on the GC2.\nStart Swing Catalyst and go to Settings (from the main screen, click the gear icon bottom left), select** Hardware.**\nEnable Launch Monitor integration. Make sure Enable as trigger is checked if you want the launch monitor to act as a capture trigger.\nSelect Foresight GC2\nExample screenshot indicating the Foresight GC2 is identified and connected:\nSimulator Integration Select ForesightSim in the Launch Monitor selection list, if it doesn’t show up automatically press “Search” to update the list.\nStart the Foresight Simulator (supported variants are: FSX, FSX 2020, \u0026 FR-1).\nNavigate to the Foresight Simulator settings, in the “On-Screen Data” section enable “Write Shots CSV” (see the simulator user manual for specifics or contact Foresight support for help with this).\nSwing Catalyst monitors the Shots.CSV file for changes and actively uses that file to pick up on shot data from the simulator.\nMake sure you’re using Club Fitting mode (only mode that will provide all ball data). Troubleshooting This section contains troubleshooting steps for the Foresight GC2 and HMT as well as the use of the GC2 with FSX.\nI just updated the software and the integration no longer works! In version 10.1.1 of Swing Catalyst, the GC2 integration is turned off by default to prevent FSX2020 from closing itself when Swing Catalyst is running. This is a temporary workaround until Foresight is able to resolve the issue with FSX.\nTo turn the GC2 integration back on, close Swing Catalyst and navigate to the Settings folder:\nC:\\ProgramData\\Swing Catalyst\\settings\nRight click on “GeneralSettings.xml” and click open with Notepad (or click Edit).\nChange false to true and save the document.\nOnce saved, start Swing Catalyst again, the GC2 should show up in the launch monitor list.\nForesight USB connection Make sure Foresight USB is selected in Swing Catalyst Settings.\nCheck the connection to the Foresight GC2 unit, and make sure the Foresight Simulator software is not running.\nIf there is missing data or shots are not picked up properly it could indicate the flash module needs replacement. Or it may be the club is missing markers or the markers are no longer working properly.\nIf you still can’t get Foresight GC2 Launch Monitor data in Swing Catalyst, please submit a ticket through our help center.\nExample screenshot showing device is connected to the computer but not fully enabled, make sure to select the device:\nForesight Simulator connection Make sure you’re receiving data in the Foresight Simulator.\nTry closing Swing Catalyst, and starting the Foresight simulator first, then start Swing Catalyst.\nMake sure that you’re using Club Fitting mode in the Foresight simulator, and that Shots.CSV is enabled in the Settings.\nMake sure that you have “Use as trigger” enabled in the Swing Catalyst settings.\nForesight Support: http://www.foresightsports.com/support/faqs\nLast updated: 2023-12-19 | View on official support site",
    "description": "Artikel dukungan ini menjelaskan cara menggunakan Foresight GC2 dengan Swing Catalyst.",
    "tags": [
      "Troubleshooting",
      "Usb-Camera",
      "Launch-Monitor",
      "Licensing"
    ],
    "title": "Cara menggunakan Foresight GC2 \u0026 HMT dengan Swing Catalyst",
